No they don't loop (as Adam and Robin) pointed out. The grammar can not
account for the various semantics of the brivla. In:

{ko'a te broda fu ko'e ko'i ko'o}

it is important that ko'X fill the same place regardless of how many places
{broda} has. Just as:

{mi blanu do leka ce'u na prami la buc.}

is grammatically correct although nonsensical

